#. module: product_rental
#: model:project.task.type,description:product_rental.stage_declared_loss
msgid ""
"- When creating a card in this project, please document it (a link with a "
"short 2 word summary or, if there is no other linked card, a DATE copy of "
"the conversation for example; otherwise the Management team arrives on the "
"card and doesn't know what it's about and is obliged to play Sherlocks "
"Holmes ;p\n"
"- On the \"tag\" side, in this pipe we only use \"[C/P/V] Water Damage\" or "
"\"[C/P/V] Perte livraison\" (the other tags are for the Support cards); if "
"none of these 2 cases => No tag\n"
"\n"
"----------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Process Management team :\n"
"- for Losses, in all cases the customer is charged full price, so there is "
"no impact on his 10% discount - for this, the Management team must remember "
"to tick the little box \"exempt from penalty\" on the PVC card (!!)\n"
"\n"
"In the event of a loss, the customer must be invoiced:\n"
"You have to make an invoice, it's more complex, but the template is quite "
"complete, it's just the invoice that is more tricky (see info below and "
"follow this example: https://shop.commown.coop/web?"
"&debug=#id=22054&view_type=form&model=account."
"invoice&action=208&active_id=1064\n"
"\n"
"- Then, when we have received the compensation payment, we make him validate "
"his address, if he needs accessories (to know if they have been stolen too), "
"and the colour (if necessary for FP2/FP4)\n"
"- Then we duplicate the corresponding opportunity with the details of the "
"device (and accessories) to be returned in the title of a card that we place "
"in the \"GO\" column of the corresponding sales pipe, and we generate the "
"PDF label for the Logistics team\n"
"- ATTENTION !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! when creating this card you MUST not forget to "
"uncheck the box in the \"shipment tracking\" tab\n"
"\n"
"+ Check that the correct contract is entered in the \"Contract\" area \n"
"-----------------------------------\n"
"Protocol in case of Lost Delivery :\n"
"!! In all cases you must create a \"loss\" card (with a \"loss of delivery\" "
"tag) to follow this case and store all the useful information for our "
"Management follow-up!\n"
"\n"
"A. The package never arrived at the customer's premises and the tracking "
"link is \"blocked\": \n"
"0/ First reflex: creation of the \"loss\" card \n"
"1/ Investigate -> go through Coliview + ask the customer for confirmation of "
"non-delivery\n"
"2/ Reship the material (!! if important value >5 k€ you need the "
"confirmation of the management!!) AND\n"
"- if B2C: we send a small message via the new logistics/opportunity card (= "
"duplication of the 1st one + generation of a new label in the process) to "
"inform him/her that a new parcel is leaving\n"
"- if B2B: the sales representative is pinged to inform his client\n"
"3/ Open a file via the Coliview online interface\n"
"4/ Once the case has been \"clarified\" (= for example: Colissimo requesting "
"an invoice), we send the most relevant justifications so that the date of "
"purchase is the most recent and the price (especially!) the most "
"representative of our real financial loss. (if you need help or a referee's "
"opinion, please contact Fred)\n"
"5/ If Colissimo takes us for Americans (= status announced as \"parcel "
"delivered\" and file closed when obviously this is not the case) => We go "
"through our Colissimo sales contact Hugo Bachelier\n"
"\n"
"B. The parcel has been delivered but the customer has not received "
"anything: \n"
"1/ we investigate on our side to find the proof of delivery (available in "
"theory on Coliview)\n"
"2/ we send it to the customer, insisting that they look a little further "
"than the end of their nose\n"
"3/ If they fail, we ask for a certificate on honour + that they make a "
"complaint to the Post Office\n"
"4/ Once these two points have been noted (certificate sent and file opened - "
"which can be seen from Coliview), only then do we reship a new device \n"
"5/ We also open a claim via Coliview (attaching the certificate and the "
"purchase invoice of the device)\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: product_rental
#: model:project.task.type,description:product_rental.stage_declared_theft
msgid ""
"- When you create a card in this project, please document it (a link with a "
"short summary in 2 words or, if there is no other linked card, a DATED copy "
"of the conversation for example; otherwise the Management team arrives on "
"the card and doesn't know what it's about and is obliged to play sherlocks "
"holmes ;p\n"
"- On the \"tag\" side, in this pipe we only use \"[C/P/V] Water Damage\" or "
"\"[C/P/V] Perte livraison\" (the other tags are for the Support cards); if "
"none of these 2 cases => No tag\n"
"- Box \"exempt from penalty\" : \n"
"1/ either we are in a situation where the customer pays the full amount of "
"the loss (cf. GCS or customer's wish, since in the Support protocol this "
"option is sometimes proposed), in which case it is the same as for Loss, we "
"tick the box and there is no impact on the discount\n"
"2/ either there is still a damage for Commown (customer pays nothing because "
"incident is covered by the contract; OR he only pays an excess - case of "
"Essential contracts!!), in this case the box is NOT ticked and the customer "
"loses the benefit of his discount\n"
"------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Management team process:\n"
"In the event of a theft for a PREMIUM contract:\n"
"- first we check that it is the 1st incident of this kind (if not, it is not "
"taken into account - in case of doubt, see Fred for adjudication)\n"
"- then if OK use and customise the \"theft\" template\n"
"(basically the customer has to send us a number of documents to validate the "
"shipment of a new device, which is at our charge (= 100% parte :( )\n"
"- Then when we have received everything, we make him validate his address, "
"if he needs accessories (to know if they have been stolen too), and the "
"colour (if necessary for FP2/FP4)\n"
"- Then we duplicate the corresponding opportunity (with the details of the "
"device (and accessories) to be returned in the title of a card that we place "
"in the \"GO\" column of the corresponding sales pipe\n"
"- ATTENTION !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! when creating this card you MUST not forget to "
"uncheck the box in the \"shipment tracking\" tab\n"
"\n"
"+ Check that the contract is entered in the \"Contract\" field in the "
"opportunity + Delete the \"Origin and Source\" fields \n"
"\n"
"----------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Process team Management :\n"
"In case of theft for an HO contract:\n"
"You have to make an invoice, it's more complex, but the template is quite "
"complete, it's just the invoice that is more tricky (see info below and "
"follow this example: https://shop.commown.coop/web?"
"&debug=#id=22054&view_type=form&model=account."
"invoice&action=208&active_id=1064\n"
"\n"
"- Then, when we have received the payment of the compensation, we make him "
"validate his address, if he needs accessories (to know if they have been "
"stolen too), and the colour (if necessary for FP2/FP4)\n"
"- Then we duplicate the corresponding opportunity with the details of the "
"device (and accessories) to be returned in the title of a card that we place "
"in the \"GO\" column of the corresponding sales pipe\n"
"- ATTENTION !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! when creating this card you MUST not forget to "
"uncheck the box in the \"shipment tracking\" tab\n"
"\n"
"+ Check that the contract is entered in the \"Contract\" field in the "
"opportunity + \"Origin and Source\" fields \n"
"---------------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"Internal note from the Management team:\n"
"FOR FP2 Ordinary Heroes: From Oct18 the purchase price of FPs has changed to "
"about 305€ (from 405), but it's not a good idea to display it on customer "
"invoices, so the strategy is the following (for 2019 customers in "
"particular):\n"
"- Leave 405\n"
"- Increase the obsolescence to 50%.  \n"
"- Send the FP invoice for Oct18 if needed for insurance purposes (the one "
"for order n°8) - only if requested! https://shop.commown.coop/web?"
"&debug=#id=2894&view_type=form&model=account.invoice&menu_id=143&action=211"
msgstr ""

